(4959267, 718700, 46679, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments! I was going for ambivalence with this photo, and I got the mixed feelings. Also, I didn''t expect to be among the first 10 with this. I''m gobsmacked really.<br/> <br/>To get an idea what I was photographing go to <a href="//www.flickr.com/photos/carlosferrer/sets/72057594135255515" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.flickr.com/photos/carlosferrer/sets/72057594135255515</a> on my Flickr.<br/> <br/>The how-to was easy, I bent really low to get the background nicely clean. Alas, the burning was unavoidable, since I had only basic equipment and was on a schedule (model, rain). Even the compensation in Lightroom didn''t change that.<br/> <br/>P.s. Will anyone PM me on how to change my "Photographers Comments"? Tks.<br/>P.p.s. Thanks for the tips, something''s not right on my side, don''t see the mentioned "edit" possiblility in the Photo Description ... a, well.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-09-17 19:09:40.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments! I was going for ambivalence with this photo, and I got the mixed feelings. Also, I didn''t expect to be among the first 10 with this. I''m gobsmacked really. To get an idea what I was photographing go to //www.flickr.com/photos/carlosferrer/sets/72057594135255515 on my Flickr. The how-to was easy, I bent really low to get the background nicely clean. Alas, the burning was unavoidable, since I had only basic equipment and was on a schedule (model, rain). Even the compensation in Lightroom didn''t change that. P.s. Will anyone PM me on how to change my "Photographers Comments"? Tks.P.p.s. Thanks for the tips, something''s not right on my side, don''t see the mentioned "edit" possiblility in the Photo Description ... a, well.', '2008-09-17 04:46:38.000000', '2008-09-17 20:09:40.000000', 0),
