(4961228, 718491, 27133, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nikon90s:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t understand why I was DQ? I would love for someone to show me what I did wrong?<br/>This was my first time posting something and I would like to thank everyone who commented on the shot.  I had fun taking it and would have loved to see how I would have done. <br/> <br/>Thanks for the DQ!!<br/> <br/>Jason </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Did you blur the foreground and background on the computer?</td>', 'Originally posted by nikon90s: I don''t understand why I was DQ? I would love for someone to show me what I did wrong?This was my first time posting something and I would like to thank everyone who commented on the shot.  I had fun taking it and would have loved to see how I would have done.  Thanks for the DQ!! Jason   Did you blur the foreground and background on the computer?', '2008-09-18 04:57:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4961240, 718456, 30807, '<td valign="top">You will have to stop sending this sort of entry in - or I just might have to move home to be up there. <br/> <br/>I had a problem even understanding what is happening here - how on earth can you get such a contrast in colour and mood in one shot of a sky - it looks like two completely different skies, but eventually, I see the tiny suns on the left, and reckoned it must be the sun actually on the left, hidden behind clouds which allow the orange sunset type glow, while on the right, it is somehow reflected and filtered or a clearer passageway to a darker night sky, with no reflections from the filtered sunset light. Well, I know what I mean anyway. <br/> <br/>To me, a simply amazing atmosphere shot - I would love to be there to capture this sort of sky - I never get anything like that where I live - it must be the thin clear air where you are which can allow this sort of image - very well captured, and I like the boat which adds scale and interest. Never mind the title, just keep sending these lovely shots in - thanks for submitting!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-09-18 04:10:45.</i></td>', 'You will have to stop sending this sort of entry in - or I just might have to move home to be up there.  I had a problem even understanding what is happening here - how on earth can you get such a contrast in colour and mood in one shot of a sky - it looks like two completely different skies, but eventually, I see the tiny suns on the left, and reckoned it must be the sun actually on the left, hidden behind clouds which allow the orange sunset type glow, while on the right, it is somehow reflected and filtered or a clearer passageway to a darker night sky, with no reflections from the filtered sunset light. Well, I know what I mean anyway.  To me, a simply amazing atmosphere shot - I would love to be there to capture this sort of sky - I never get anything like that where I live - it must be the thin clear air where you are which can allow this sort of image - very well captured, and I like the boat which adds scale and interest. Never mind the title, just keep sending these lovely shots in - thanks for submitting!', '2008-09-18 05:09:03.000000', '2008-09-18 05:10:45.000000', 0),
