(4970170, 720069, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Carl,<br/>       I like the title and the image is a unique take on this challange &amp; fits well. I like the placement of the elements &amp; the image seems to be in focus. With that being said for me the over all image just seems a little bland to me. Imho there are three things that stuck me instantly. 1) The over all image just seems a bit featureless, A bit more detail in the trees &amp; ground cover would have helped a great deal here. 2) The tonality of the over all image seems very clumped, everything just seems to blend together this inclueds the person kneeling. 3) The sky, it just kept competeting for my eye, this was a direct result of the blending around your main subject &amp; through out the image too contrasty for me. Over all this image has great potential it had that erie feeling of ventureing into the unknown &amp; was well framed. With a few adjustments this image could be dynomite.</td>', 'Hi Carl,       I like the title and the image is a unique take on this challange & fits well. I like the placement of the elements & the image seems to be in focus. With that being said for me the over all image just seems a little bland to me. Imho there are three things that stuck me instantly. 1) The over all image just seems a bit featureless, A bit more detail in the trees & ground cover would have helped a great deal here. 2) The tonality of the over all image seems very clumped, everything just seems to blend together this inclueds the person kneeling. 3) The sky, it just kept competeting for my eye, this was a direct result of the blending around your main subject & through out the image too contrasty for me. Over all this image has great potential it had that erie feeling of ventureing into the unknown & was well framed. With a few adjustments this image could be dynomite.', '2008-09-23 15:31:35.000000', NULL, 0),
